Z||000009||LarryB||10-18-2001||01:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR><B>WAN is Wide Area Network<BR>Kinda like if you have a network connected to another network in a building on the side of town.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That configuration nowadays would be know as part of a MAN, or Metropolitan Area Network.<P>(And no, I'm not kidding.)<P>WAN is typically used now to describe a network built using intercity, or LD (Long Distance) fiber. <P><BR>||||reg||1
